<title>USA: Novartis' Actigall cleared for prevention.</title>
<headline>Novartis' Actigall cleared for prevention.</headline>
<dateline>EAST HANOVER, N.J. 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Novartis Pharmaceuticals Corp said Wednesday that its Actigall has been cleared by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for the prevention of gallstones in obese patients experiencing rapid weight loss.</p>
<p>According to the company, Actigall is the first medication indicated for the prevention of gallstones in these patients.</p>
<p>It has been used for treatment of gallstones since 1988.</p>
</text>
